     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Social/Emotional:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " plays games with you, like pat‑a‑cake. "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Language/Communication:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " waves \"bye‑bye\"; calls a parent \"mama\" or \"dada\" or another special name; understands \"no\" (pauses briefly or stops). "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Cognitive:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " puts something in a container (a block in a cup); looks for things he sees you hide. "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Movement/Physical:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " pulls up to stand; walks holding on to furniture; drinks from a cup without a lid as you hold it; picks things up between thumb and pointer finger (pincer grasp). [S3] "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "italic"
       }
      ],
      "text": "(Bright Futures surveillance adds, per S2: uses \"Dada\"/\"Mama\" specifically; uses 1 word other than Mama/Dada; follows directions with gestures; takes first independent steps; stands without support; drops an object in a cup; picks up food to eat.)"
     }
